-- title:
--   Full-response assembly and the complete affine sampler program
-- statement:
--   The full-response and finite-rectangle programs assemble the sampler numerical data. The tape codec divides a padded public random bit string into the independent components used by proposal generation, bounded rejection, chart completion, and affine emission. The complete program reads the platform sampler request and returns the encoded integer matrix and offset. Later theorems prove its polynomial running time, invertibility, and Gaussian transport accuracy.
-- source:
--   Companion Lean implementation for the fixed-family Gaussian affine transport theorem. The source modules and their SHA-256 hashes are recorded in the checked extraction manifest. This exact generated file has SHA-256 dd646234e1579316961f7ee691d5052073a179c75157646c463926ebacefe58f. Source modules: Integration9_9_TM2NativeChoiceAverage, Integration9_9_TM2NativeCompletion, Integration9_9_TM2NativeFullResponse, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRadix, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRectangleDecode, Integration9_9_TM2NativeFullResponseMatrix, Integration9_9_TM2NativeRectangle, Integration9_9_TM2NativeProducer, Integration9_9_TM2NativeTapeCodec, Integration9_9_TM2NativeTapeLengths, Integration9_9_TM2NativeTapeSeed, Integration9_9_TM2NativeTapeCore, Integration9_9_TM2NativeTapes, Integration9_9_TM2NativeSampler, Integration9_9_TM2NativeSamplerRequest. Alternate sparse native dependencies preserve the original non-import body bytes and all public types; this header-only packaging is recorded in sparse_live/manifest.json. Current source SHA256 d4d5d1755c1d024dabf9865b6065892b5ba296778daa1c81bbd08fe35cddda57. Native10/11 split fallback keeps every original scope-closed data body unchanged and retains the canonical module names as import facades. Current source SHA256 d4d5d1755c1d024dabf9865b6065892b5ba296778daa1c81bbd08fe35cddda57.

